{
  "item": "A",
  "tickets": ["EBA-440"],
  "description": "BTPS 1.1 item A, lifecycle events carried as BTPS_EVENT (release plan page 10518529, section 2). Each case names an event in events/ (or a document as documents/<name>), optionally changed by `set` (top-level fields replaced) and `unset` (top-level fields removed). schema: the SDK's parseBtpEventDoc accepts or refuses it. envelope: validateBtpEventEnvelope against a BTPS_EVENT from `from` to `to` whose id is the event's id (or `artifactId`): one id end to end, and only a document between the two parties. chains: each step parses and passes its envelope; a step that starts a chain has no inReplyTo; every reply passes validateBtpEventReply against the step its inReplyTo names (the receiving platform's check, section 2.7). A chain expected to be refused fails at its last step. Every event is also checked to be unchanged by parsing, and signed and verified over its JCS form on every runtime. Document sha256 values are illustrative: the protocol never recomputes them.",
